usage: mlb_02_games_scrape.py [-h] --season SEASON [--root ROOT]
                              [--max-games MAX_GAMES] [--workers WORKERS]
                              [--game-types GAME_TYPES]

Stage 02 -- capture: one feed/live payload per completed game.
``mlb/raw/{season}/{game_pk}.json.gz``. File-exists resumable, so a re-run
after a partial night costs nothing and re-fetches nothing -- the same
contract the NCAA stages hold. One fetch yields pbp, pitches, all three box
tables, officials and linescore, so those datasets are free at build time
rather than extra requests. Measured 2026-09-09 through the ProxyBonanza pool:
0.68 s mean sequential, 11.4 games/s at 8 workers, 26.4 at 16, with zero
rejections across ~150 requests. Default is 8; 16 is 26 req/s at one host and
is not the polite default.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --season SEASON
  --root ROOT
  --max-games MAX_GAMES
                        cap per run (0 = all)
  --workers WORKERS     default 8 (SDV_MLB_WORKERS)
  --game-types GAME_TYPES
                        comma-separated statsapi gameType codes (default:
                        regular season + postseason; spring
                        training/exhibition/all-star excluded)
EXIT=0
